WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
SPEAKER: Creating a good
user experience for customers

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.070
and the teams that
maintain a chatbot agent

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.180
are both very important.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.290
And so in this episode of
Deconstructing Chatbots,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.360
we will share seven
best practices that

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.730
will tie in key
pro moves you may

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.240
have seen in our prior lessons,
but we'll touch more upon now.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.296
So stay tuned.

00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:23.208
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.410
The first step is
to future-proof

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.700
the names of intents.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.220
As your agent supports a
greater variety of topics,

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.850
the more successful the
collaboration with others

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.700
will be by using explicit names.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.620
A common practice
is to format them

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.550
as your intention
dot expected action.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.740
Four common examples
of these intents

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.070
are for information
collection, confirmation,

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:55.090
supplemental questions, and
redirecting to live agents.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.410
Let's go through each.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.390
For example, when
collecting information

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.330
for helping a customer to
purchase shoes for their pups,

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.970
you can name your
intent shoes dot book

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.840
to collect parameters
such as color and size.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.630
Next, as a user navigates
through your flows,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.780
it's good to confirm and repeat
back if the information was

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:14.970
correct or not.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.770
Ergo, having two intents
called confirmation

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.700
dot yes and confirmation
dot no are useful.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.490
And we'll talk more about these
benefits using confirmation

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.040
yes no intents in a bit.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.220
Then there are questions that
customers may have that are not

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.450
core to your purchasing
flow, but you

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.390
know are frequently asked.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.790
Let's call these supplementals.

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:40.360
For example, customers are more
interested in sustainability

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.160
and frequently ask Pugs--

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.500
are your products
sustainably sourced?

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.080
Or may have questions
about their account.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.280
And as a fourth type of intent,
known as redirect dot support

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.530
team, is meant to
allow customers

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.980
to eject out of the flow
to speak to a live person.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:01.780
Next, let's talk about reusing
intents and pages via the route

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.760
group functionality.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.880
By designing your agent
with reusability in mind,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.630
it helps save time answering
the same intent from anywhere

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.980
in the journey.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.500
You can do this by
creating multiple intents

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.220
and putting them together
in a route group once.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.670
And just modify every page
to allow for that same group

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:22.720
to be used.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.470
For example, you can put
100 supplemental intents

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.650
at the beginning of
the flow and at the end

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.230
during the confirmation
pages to enable

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.990
users to ask questions
outside of the flow

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.885
and be brought back to the
flow after getting answers.

00:02:37.885 --> 00:02:40.635
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.190
Next, you can train your
agent with phrases in bulk

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.880
by uploading them.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.390
This can be done by
visiting the desired intent

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:07.943
and clicking the Upload icon
to upload a CSV or txt file.

00:03:07.943 --> 00:03:11.120
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.750
Next tip is to add rephrased
variations of questions

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.910
when you have
required parameters,

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.550
since it will not stop
asking this question

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.960
until it gets collected.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:24.920
And it's good to rephrase the
question up to three times,

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.140
then to pass a
customer to a human

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.790
to avoid a bad user experience
if the third try doesn't help.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.820
This is a great rule of thumb,
by the way, that all of us

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.430
have experienced at
some point as consumers.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:40.358
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.210
And for yes/no questions,
you want to say,

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.010
did I get that right?

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.940
And leverage the confirmation
dot yes or no intents.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.920
This brings us to
the next point.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.110
It's beneficial to
reduce ambiguity

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.630
by repeating back
what a person heard,

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.610
as it builds trust
with the user.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:12.330
Ergo, by using the money symbol
and the name of the entity

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.340
in the fulfillment
section, which

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.920
is the reply to the
customer by the agent,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.240
you can reaffirm to the customer
what was understood from them.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.370
This applies to both
the extensive list

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:27.030
of system entities built into
dialogue flows such as color

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.630
or date, for example,
or custom ones you

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:33.810
build that you do not find as
a system entity, such as size.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.870
Next, to enable a user to
erase their past intent,

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.080
for example--

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.730
I want red shoes.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:40.230
Oh, wait.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.640
Never mind.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.030
You make an intent route
called "go back" and make

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.314
the parameter ask to null.

00:04:47.314 --> 00:04:50.218
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.060
And finally, it's important
to be testing your agent

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.160
as frequently as
possible when building it

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.310
bit by bit to catch
errors faster.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.430
You can do this by going to
the test agent functionality

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.241
on the top right side.

00:05:10.241 --> 00:05:12.696
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.260
And there you have it--

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.320
seven best practices for
building a robust agent that

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.380
creates a positive user
experience both for end

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.170
users and those who've
maintained the agent.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.050
I hope to see you in the next
episode for deconstructing

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:30.860
chatbots.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.750
If you like this
video and would like

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.940
to see more of
such content, don't

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.940
forget to like and subscribe,
as well as to check out

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.970
the helpful links I have listed
in this video subscription.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:43.310
Cheers, and thank
you for watching.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

